    "lawCode": "Amd §§2581 & 207, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S629\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to lymphedema\n\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis legislation would require healthcare providers that report cases\nof cancer or other malignant disease to also include instances of\nlymphedema in patients coming under their care. This legislation would\nalso require information be provided to cancer patients seeking\nvarious treatments of post-treatment risks such as lymphedema.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 2400 of the public health law is amended; §2. Subdivisions 1\nand 3 of section 2401 of the public health law, as amended by chapter\n642 of the laws of 1997 are amended; §3. Section 2404 of the public\nhealth law is amended by adding a new subsection 1-b; §4. Paragraph\n(c) of subdivision 1 of section 2404-a of the public health law; as\nadded by chapter 141 of the laws of 1997 is amended; and, §5.\nSubdivision 1 of section 2581 of the public health law, as amended by\nchapter 654 of the laws of 1986 is amended.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThis bill requires that health care providers that report cases of\ncancer or other malignant disease to also include instances of\nlymphedema in patients coming under their care. This legislation would\nalso require information be provided to cancer patients seeking\nvarious treatments of post-treatment risks such as lymphedema.\n\nLymphedema is an accumulation of lymphatic fluid in the interstitial\ntissue that causes swelling, most often in the arm(s) or leges), and\noccasionally in other parts of the body, Lymphedema can develop when\nlymphatic vessels are missing or impaired (primary), or when lymph\nvessels are damaged or lymph nodes removed (secondary).\n\nRadiation therapy, used in the treatment of various cancers and some\nAIDS-related diseases, can damage the normal flow of the lymphatic\nnodes and vessels causing scar tissue to form which interrupts the\nnormal flow of the lymphatic fluid.\n\nMoreover, untreated, lymphedema can lead into a decrease or loss of\nfunctioning of the limbs, skin breakdown, and chronic infections.  In\nmost cases, untreated lymphedema can develop into a rare form of\nlymphatic cancer.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n2006: A.11078\n2007-2008: S.3248-B/A.5892-B Passed the Assembly\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
